
sequenceDiagram
    %% ==Checkout & Payment Sequence: guest browse → auth → cart → order → Stripe payment → webhook → fulfillment
    autonumber
    actor U as "Customer"
    actor A as "Staff / Admin"
    participant FE as "Frontend"
    participant NG as "nginx (ecommerce-nginx)"
    participant API as "FastAPI (ecommerce-api)"
    participant DB as "Postgres (ecommerce-db)"
    participant RD as "Redis (db1: blacklist)"
    participant CW as "Celery Worker (emails queue)"
    participant SM as "SMTP / Mailpit"
    participant ST as "Stripe"

    %% ============ 1. REGISTRATION & AUTH ============
    Note over U,ST: 1. Registration & Email Verification
    U->>FE: Register (email, password)
    FE->>NG: POST /api/v1/auth/register
    NG->>API: proxy → auth router
    API->>API: AuthService.register (argon2/bcrypt hash)
    API->>DB: INSERT User (role=customer, is_verified=false)
    API-->>CW: send_verification_email.delay() (queue: emails)
    CW->>SM: verification email (24h token, type=verify)
    SM-->>U: verification link
    U->>FE: Open link → POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email {token}
    API->>API: decode token, type=verify
    API->>DB: UPDATE User SET is_verified=true
    API-->>U: 200 OK — account verified

    Note over U,ST: 2. Login (JWT access + rotating refresh token)
    U->>FE: Login (email, password)
    FE->>NG: POST /api/v1/auth/login (rate limited 10/min)
    NG->>API: AuthService.login
    API->>DB: SELECT User by email
    API->>API: verify password hash
    API->>RD: refresh jti registered on logout/rotation only
    API-->>FE: 200 {access_token (15min, type=access), refresh_token (7d, jti)}<br/>+ HttpOnly SameSite=strict cookie

    Note over U,ST: 3. Token Refresh (rotation + Redis blacklist)
    FE->>NG: POST /api/v1/auth/refresh (cookie / X-Refresh-Token header)
    NG->>API: AuthService.refresh
    API->>RD: GET token_blacklist: {jti}
    alt jti blacklisted or invalid
        API-->>FE: 401 Unauthorized
    else valid
        API->>RD: SETEX token_blacklist: {old_jti} (remaining TTL)
        API-->>FE: new access_token + new refresh_token (rotated cookie)
    end

    %% ============ 2. CART ============
    Note over U,ST: 4. Shopping Cart (guest session → user cart merge)
    U->>FE: Add item to cart (guest)
    FE->>NG: POST /api/v1/cart/items
    NG->>API: CartService.add_item (signed cart_session_id cookie)
    API->>DB: validate ProductVariant stock (stock_quantity ≥ qty)
    API->>DB: INSERT/UPDATE CartItem
    API-->>U: cart with subtotal

    U->>FE: Login → POST /api/v1/cart/merge
    API->>DB: fold guest cart items into user cart

    %% ============ 3. ORDER CREATION ============
    Note over U,ST: 5. Order Creation (stock decrement + totals)
    U->>FE: Checkout → POST /api/v1/orders {shipping_address_id, coupon_code?}
    FE->>NG: Bearer access token
    NG->>API: OrderService.create_order
    API->>DB: validate address belongs to user, load cart items
    API->>DB: check stock → snapshot OrderItems (name, unit_price)<br/>→ DECREMENT ProductVariant.stock_quantity
    API->>API: PricingService.calculate_order_totals<br/>(subtotal − SAVE10 discount + 8% tax + shipping: free ≥ $50 else $5)
    API->>DB: INSERT Order (status=pending) → DELETE cart items
    API-->>CW: send_order_confirmation_email.delay(order.id, total, email)
    CW->>SM: "Your order is paid" email
    API-->>FE: 201 OrderOut {order_id, status=pending, total}

    %% ============ 4. PAYMENT ============
    Note over U,ST: 6. Payment Intent (idempotency-guarded)
    U->>FE: Pay → POST /api/v1/payments/intent {order_id}
    FE->>NG: Bearer access token
    NG->>API: PaymentService.create_payment_intent
    API->>DB: order must be pending & owned by user
    alt Payment already exists for order
        API->>ST: retrieve existing PaymentIntent
        ST-->>API: existing client_secret (no duplicate charge)
    else first attempt
        API->>ST: PaymentIntent.create(amount, currency, idempotency_key=uuid4())
        ST-->>API: PaymentIntent (client_secret)
        API->>DB: INSERT Payment (status=pending, provider_payment_id, unique idempotency_key)
    end
    API-->>FE: 200 {client_secret}

    %% ============ 5. STRIPE WEBHOOK ============
    Note over U,ST: 7. Stripe Webhook (async payment confirmation)
    U->>ST: Confirm card payment (client-side Stripe.js)
    ST->>NG: POST /api/v1/payments/webhook (Stripe-Signature header)
    NG->>API: stripe.Webhook.construct_event (signature verification)
    alt payment_intent.succeeded
        API->>DB: Payment pending→succeeded<br/>Order pending→paid (VALID_TRANSITIONS)
        API-->>CW: send_order_status_email.delay(order.id, paid)
        CW->>SM: "Your order is paid" email
    else payment_intent.payment_failed / charge.failed
        API->>DB: Payment pending→failed (store failure_message)
        API-->>U: customer retries payment or cancels order
    end

    %% ============ 6. FULFILLMENT ============
    Note over U,ST: 8. Fulfillment by Staff / Admin (state machine)
    A->>FE: PATCH /api/v1/orders/{id}/status (staff token)
    FE->>NG: require_staff_or_admin
    NG->>API: OrderService.update_status
    API->>DB: validate transition<br/>(paid→processing→shipped→delivered / →refunded, →cancelled)
    API->>DB: UPDATE Order status
    API-->>CW: send_order_status_email.delay(order.id, new_status)
    CW->>SM: status update email
    API-->>A: 200 OrderOut

    Note over U,ST: 9. Refund (admin, Stripe)
    A->>FE: POST /api/v1/payments/orders/{id}/refund
    API->>ST: Refund.create(charge_id)
    ST-->>API: refund succeeded
    API->>DB: Payment → refunded, Order → refunded
    API-->>CW: send_order_status_email.delay(order.id, refunded)
    CW->>SM: refund confirmation email

    %% ============ 7. LOGOUT ============
    Note over U,ST: 10. Logout (refresh token blacklisting)
    U->>FE: Logout
    FE->>NG: POST /api/v1/auth/logout
    NG->>API: AuthService.logout
    API->>RD: SETEX token_blacklist: {refresh_jti}
    API-->>FE: 200 + delete refresh cookie